sted2 (2.07m+20010303+a06.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Revival of the Linux port for modern 64-bit systems
    (https://github.com/rtanote/sted2); packaging taken over from the
    archived Debian package.
  * Fix 64-bit _dos_malloc sentinel, GCC >= 14 build, X11 restore without
    a compositor, Ctrl+G score-view glyphs, and signed-char flat-key input
    on ARM (see README.md for details).
  * Ship FluidSynth integration: sted2 launcher auto-connects snd-virmidi
    to FluidSynth, sted2-play plays SMF via aplaymidi.
  * Modernize packaging: debhelper-compat 13, dh sequencer, source format
    3.0 (native), current build dependency names.
  * Install the real binary and data to /usr/lib/sted with the launcher in
    /usr/bin; keep user-editable config in /etc/sted2 via symlinks, with
    group-audio write access managed by dpkg-statoverride.

 -- rtagaya <rtagaya@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0900

